WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:06.290
HERE'S WHAT YOU DIDN'T KNOW ABOUT THE AT&amp;T
COMMERCIAL GIRL

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.019
Everybody loves Lily, AT&amp;T's perky, enthusiastic
commercial spokeswoman.

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:16.270
Based on her TV ads, we know she's nerdy and
awkward, a hopeless romantic, and she likes

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.270
bedazzling.

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.860
But how much do you actually know about the
lady behind the Lily?

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.930
Here's what you may not have known about the
AT&amp;T commercial girl.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:25.040
MILANA VAYNTRUB

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.779
This might blow your mind, but Lily's name
isn't actually Lily.

00:00:28.779 --> 00:00:32.230
It's actually Milana Aleksandrovna Vayntrub.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:37.710
Vayntrub was born in the Uzbek Soviet Socialist
Republic, or what's now the Republic of Uzbekistan.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:41.329
You know what they say: give us your tired,
your poor, and your huddled masses yearning

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:45.530
to become Hollywood pop-culture sensations.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.530
POLITICAL REFUGEE

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.559
Life in the USSR wasn't exactly sunshine and
rainbows for the Vayntrubs, especially because

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:55.760
they faced persistent religious persecution
for being Jewish in an officially atheist

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:56.760
country.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:01.149
When Milana was two, her family fled Uzbekistan
in hopes of finding religious freedom and

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:03.239
political asylum in America.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:07.159
The process was long and grueling, with the
family stranded in both Austria and Italy

00:01:07.159 --> 00:01:08.250
for a while.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.280
Luckily, the Vayntrubs made it to America
and settled in California, which sounds like

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.280
a wonderful step up.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.930
BARBIE AND ER

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.549
Lily is hardly the first character Vayntrub
ever played in a commercial.

00:01:19.549 --> 00:01:24.030
She began acting in TV ads at five, starring
in Barbie commercials to help her family make

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.030
ends meet.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.930
Her first big break happened in 1995, when
she landed a guest spot on ER, where she appeared

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.799
alongside stars like Julianna Margulies at
the precocious and precious age of eight!

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:36.509
HIGH SCHOOL DROPOUT

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:40.409
Vayntrub attended Beverly Hills High School,
but she dropped out as a sophomore.

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:42.950
But not because she didn't value her education.

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.270
She actually wanted to learn more quickly.

00:01:45.270 --> 00:01:50.369
Vayntrub got her GED and moved on to the University
of San Diego, where she earned a degree in

00:01:50.369 --> 00:01:54.420
communication—appropriate considering she's
known for selling AT&amp;T products.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.270
UCB GRAD

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:00.899
The Upright Citizen's Brigade is one of the
most famous comedy troupes in show business.

00:02:00.899 --> 00:02:05.469
Vayntrub honed her comedy chops with the UCB,
joining other famous graduates like Saturday

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:10.420
Night Live vets Kate McKinnon, Bobby , and
Horatio Sanz, to name only a few.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.750
She may not have made the SNL cast yet, but
her work with the UCB helps explain her comedic

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:16.820
timing.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.810
YOUTUBE SENSATION

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:23.470
Vayntrub has guest starred on shows like Key
and Peele, Californication, and Silicon Valley.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.000
But before all that, she rose to prominence
through a different channel—on YouTube.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.970
As one of the co-creators of Live Prude Girls,
Vayntrub was an early YouTube sensation, with

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:35.890
each of her videos earning hundreds of thousands
of views.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:39.770
The channel is dormant now, but if you want
a sneak peek at life before Lily, you can

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:42.390
still watch Vayntrub's hit videos online.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.440
Bonus points if you watch from an AT&amp;T device...

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.510
THE CAN'T DO NOTHING MOVEMENT

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.760
Vayntrub created the "Can't Do Nothing" movement,
which has spurred nearly a quarter of a million

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.000
people worldwide to use social media to help
crusade for the rights of refugees around

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.000
the globe.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.850
Saving the world by using your AT&amp;T phone
to record YouTube videos of yourself helping

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:01.850
refugees?

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.890
That's just the kind of moment Lily would
absolutely love.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:06.890
Thanks for watching!

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:10.410
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.810
And leave us a comment to share your favorite
Lily moment!

